{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/59","id":4687141761,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF2AbgQ","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/59","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/59.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/59.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/59","number":59,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"research(10300025): credited line-action result with source-scope warning","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Exact scope\n\nRecords an affirmative answer to the literal per-element additive-distortion condition in Calegari's Question 8.2. This is a credited consequence of known line-action conjugacy results, not a new discovery.\n\nDeroin–Kleptsyn–Navas–Parwani, Ann. Probab. 41 (2013), Theorem 8.5, gives a stronger conclusion for finitely generated orientation-preserving actions. The package includes self-contained deterministic proofs of the needed weaker conclusion, including a countable-family, orientation-reversing extension. All maps use one common coordinate change.\n\nThe historical toroidal-obstruction remark is explicitly retained as a mismatch with the displayed quantifiers. No bound uniform across group elements, geometric control of the conjugacy, or ambient leaf-distance conclusion is asserted.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 6,665 exact rational author controls\n- Separate adversarial AI review PASS, with 20,173 independent exact checks\n- Full original problem PDF, earlier published formulation and current published-theorem reprint checked\n- No novelty claim or new-solution campaign credit\n\nRecommended queue classification: `already_solved` for the literal statement. The parent coordinates the queue row; this branch changes only the problem's attempt directory.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T07:08:50Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:10:47Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"26d4bae1b4f32792f95b6f0338d079b619a8b7de","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/59/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/59/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/59/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/bdee508c676c98cb96dbc1a2e5aef2fe9cd1c744","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-10300025","ref":"dot/math-10300025","sha":"bdee508c676c98cb96dbc1a2e5aef2fe9cd1c744","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/fo